  "accessibility": {
    "title": "One feature, end to end",
    "description": "You ask the coding agent for a specification for passwordless sign-in; it asks only the questions that change the outcome and writes the specification under .planr/. You ask for a plan; it writes user stories and tasks, and the planr CLI validates the cross-references offline. You ship one task at a time: the agent reads the plan first, implements and verifies the task, and records provenance; you open one pull request per task, GitHub runs CI and review, land prepares the exact merge commands, and you merge. Release writes the release entry and operate returns a readout that becomes evidence for the next specification.",
